# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what the Dockerfile COPYs.
#
# The build context is sent to the Docker daemon (and cached by BuildKit) in full. The working
# tree holds client documents ("AI Test/", samples/), Docling's parse of them (.eval_cache/),
# evaluation scores (eval_runs/), .env with secrets, the SQLite database and uploads (data/),
# and multi-GB models. A deny-list has to name every one of those and silently leaks the next
# one somebody adds; an allowlist cannot. If the Dockerfile gains a COPY, add a line here.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/
!scripts/supervise.py

# Re-included directories can still carry build debris.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
